Initial armaments would include two classic six-shooters, an ammo belt
(with a random number of rounds), a bulletproof vest, and a bitchin'
cowboy hat.  The Gunslinger would (obviously) need to reload after the
emptying the six-shooters.  Firing on most creatures, a shot to the head
would result in sudden death or severe injury (regardless of HP). 
Creatures without heads or protected by metal helmets would be impervious
to head shots.  The likelihood of a head shot would be determined by
Dex and skill level with the weapon.  New items would need to be
implemented to accommodate the new character class. Ammo and various types
of rifles and pistols are what I have in mind. For example, starting out
the Gunslinger would be equipped with two standard six-shooters, but a
Beretta (capable of faster output and greater ammo capacity) might be
available somewhere in the game.  Other, more powerful weaponry would also
be generated randomly throughout the dungeon.

Reason, of Snow Crash fame, could be wielded by the Gunslinger and would
be among the most powerful armaments held by him.  Most armor would be
completely useless against Reason, with a few notable exceptions.  Reason
would be quite difficult to acquire, and ammo for it would be extremely
rare (perhaps the target of a /ofW?).  Sniper rifles, capable of accurate
long-ranged attacks (subject to skill level), could also be wielded by the
Gunslinger.  Tranquilizer weapons could take the place of a /ofSleep. 
This dependence on ranged attacks would put the Gunslinger in danger.  The
Gunslinger's main weakness would be his low Str rate and his
vulnuerability to melee attacks.  A low Con rate could also be barrier to
the Gunslinger's power, given most RL Gunslingers apparent inability to
heal themselves properly.  

